{
  "$comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC TEST FIXTURE - not tenant output. No tenant exists for this lab; no access review has run.",
    "Input for 10-Review-KPIs.ps1 -InputPath and tests/10-Review-KPIs.Tests.ps1. Shapes follow Graph v1.0 (accessReviewScheduleDefinition / instance / accessReviewInstanceDecisionItem; assignment policies reduced to id + package + automatic).",
    "Built to hit every ADR 0012 KPI: a 2-second bulk approver (rubber stamp), approvals against a Deny recommendation with and without justification, unanswered items, a system-applied default, a review of BIRTHRIGHT access (T3) that locks out two nurses, a mover whose denial is NOT a lockout, an expiry lockout, an out-of-lookback instance and an unclassified review.",
    "Expected: T1 completion 100.0, T2 88.2 (target 95 missed), rubber-stamp 50.0 % (1 of 2 eligible reviewers), clinical lockouts 2 (review 1, expiry 1) -> exit 2.",
    "Lockouts by review: Grace (T3 review of the legacy Nurse request policy, system-applied Deny). NOT lockouts: u-float03 - a float nurse since hired into ICU (HR: ICU / Registered Nurse) whose 'ICU - Float Access' assignment a T2 review denied. Since the ICU split that removes only the float package; her ICU birthright package comes from the automatic policy and no review can touch it (before the split the same Deny removed the ICU package itself - the transition lockout ADR 0012 warns about). Dana's T3 Deny: she still holds the package through a Delivered assignment. u-float04 (default-applied Deny, attributes unknown): outside T3 only people KNOWN to be in birthright scope count.",
    "The two T2 reviews stand for the T2 packages ADR 0012 still reviews (an extendable or longer-than-180-day variant); a plain 180-day T2 package is certified by its expiry and gets no campaign."
  ],
